AWS Cloud Infrastructure Final Project
Overview

This project demonstrates the deployment of cloud infrastructure within Amazon Web Services (AWS). The objective was to design and implement a secure environment by creating networking components and deploying an EC2 instance.

Project Objectives
Select an AWS Region
Create a Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)
Create a Subnet
Create and configure a Security Group
Generate an EC2 Key Pair
Deploy and configure an EC2 Instance
Implement IAM best practices using an administrative user
AWS Services Used
AWS IAM
Amazon VPC
Amazon EC2
Security Groups
Key Pairs
Elastic Block Store (EBS)
Project Implementation
Step 1: Region Selection

Selected Region: N. Virginia (us-east-1)

The region was selected based on proximity, low latency, and service availability.

Step 2: Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)

Created a custom VPC using:

IPv4 CIDR Block: 10.0.0.0/16
Step 3: Subnet Configuration

Created a subnet within the VPC using:

CIDR Block: 10.0.1.0/24

The subnet was configured as a public subnet through Internet Gateway and Route Table configuration.

Step 4: Key Pair and Security Group

Key Pair:

Created and downloaded a PEM key file for secure SSH access.

Security Group:

Allowed SSH access (TCP Port 22)
Source: 0.0.0.0/0
Step 5: EC2 Deployment

Configuration:

AMI: Amazon Linux
Instance Type: t2.micro
Network: Custom VPC
Subnet: Public Subnet
Auto Assign Public IP: Enabled
Security Group: Custom Security Group

The instance was successfully launched and connected using the generated key pair.

